imx95-navqb: add Neutron NPU DMA pool (reserved-memory)

The base imx95.dtsi neutron node ships with no memory-region. NXP enables the
NPU on the i.MX95 EVK via the imx95-19x19-evk-neutron.dtso overlay, which the
NavQ device tree never applies. Without a DMA pool the Neutron NPU loads its
firmware and clocks up, but an inference never completes: the completion IRQ
(GIC_SPI 318 == Linux GICv3 350, "imx-neutron-mailbox") never fires and the eIQ
Neutron TFLite delegate returns "Neutron Driver timeout (code=1497)".

Add the same pool here in the navqb board dts so it lands in imx95-navqb.dtb
(u-boot auto-selects that dtb by board name, so no boot-path change is needed).
NavQ95 has >=8 GiB and u-boot fixes up the memory node at runtime, so the EVK's
4 GiB pool at 0x1_0000_0000 fits above every existing reservation with no
collision. "reusable" makes it a shared-dma CMA pool, available to the system
until the NPU claims it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NavQ95 board integration; should be fixed in NXP-Robotics/linux-imx]
Signed-off-by: Leonardo Bornia <leonardo.bornia@toradex.com>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-navqb.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-navqb.dts
@@ -1032,3 +1032,29 @@
 };
 
 
+
+/*
+ * Neutron NPU DMA pool. Mirror of NXP's imx95-19x19-evk-neutron.dtso, applied
+ * here in the board dts so it lands in imx95-navqb.dtb (u-boot auto-selects
+ * that dtb by board name; no boot-path change needed).
+ *
+ * The base imx95.dtsi neutron node has no memory-region, so without this pool
+ * the NPU loads its firmware and clocks up but an inference never completes:
+ * the completion IRQ (GIC_SPI 318 == Linux GICv3 350, "imx-neutron-mailbox")
+ * never fires and the delegate returns "Neutron Driver timeout". NavQ95 has
+ * >=8 GiB (u-boot fixes up the memory node at runtime), so the EVK's 4 GiB pool
+ * at 0x1_0000_0000 fits above all existing reservations with no collision.
+ * "reusable" makes it a shared-dma CMA pool, usable by the system until the
+ * NPU claims it.
+ */
+&{/reserved-memory} {
+	neutron_mem: neutron_memory@100000000 {
+		compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
+		reusable;
+		reg = <0x1 0x00000000 0x1 0x00000000>;
+	};
+};
+
+&neutron {
+	memory-region = <&neutron_mem>;
+};
